name":"edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/yarin.b/projects/excel_magic/artifacts/runs/20261002T174654Z_J6_qwen-code_breast_cancer/workspace/pipeline.py","new_string":"\"\"\"Candidate data pipeline around a FROZEN tabular foundation model.\n\nThe harness calls, in order:\n  1. preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test)        -> X_train, y_train, X_test   (cleaning, target transform)\n  2. engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test)          -> X_train, X_test            (feature engineering, <= 500 cols)\n  3. sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows)  -> list of index arrays       (context views; each view is fit separately\n                                                                                 and predictions are averaged)\n  4. frozen model fit/predict per view (never edit this part; MODEL_KWARGS tunes the constructor)\n  5. postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test)     -> pred                       (invert target transforms, calibrate)\n\n`pred` is a pandas DataFrame of class probabilities (columns = class labels) for classification, or a\npandas Series for regression. `y_train_orig` is the untransformed training target. All inputs are pandas\nobjects; X_train / X_test share columns. Do not read any file other than the ones in this directory.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # No preprocessing needed for this dataset\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create engineered features based on domain knowledge for breast cancer classification\n    \n    # Ratio features that might capture differences between benign and malignant tumors\n    # Size ratios\n    X_train['area_perimeter_ratio'] = X_train['mean area'] / (X_train['mean perimeter'] + 1e-8)\n    X_test['area_perimeter_ratio'] = X_test['mean area'] / (X_test['mean perimeter'] + 1e-8)\n    \n    # Shape complexity features\n    X_train['concavity_points_ratio'] = X_train['mean concavity'] / (X_train['mean concave points'] + 1e-8)\n    X_test['concavity_points_ratio'] = X_test['mean concavity'] / (X_test['mean concave points'] + 1e-8)\n    \n    # Compactness features\n    X_train['compactness_ratio'] = X_train['mean compactness'] / (X_train['mean concavity'] + 1e-8)\n    X_test['compactness_ratio'] = X_test['mean compactness'] / (X_test['mean concavity'] + 1e-8)\n    \n    # Spread features (difference between worst and mean)\n    X_train['radius_spread'] = X_train['worst radius'] - X_train['mean radius']\n    X_test['radius_spread'] = X_test['worst radius'] - X_test['mean radius']\n    \n    X_train['area_spread'] = X_train['worst area'] - X_train['mean area']\n    X_test['area_spread'] = X_test['worst area'] - X_test['mean area']\n    \n    # Log-transformed features for skewed distributions\n    X_train['log_area'] = np.log1p(X_train['mean area'])\n    X_test['log_area'] = np.log1p(X_test['mean area'])\n    \n    X_train['log_perimeter'] = np.log1p(X_train['mean perimeter'])\n    X_test['log_perimeter'] = np.log1p(X_test['mean perimeter'])\n    \n    # Combined complexity feature\n    X_train['complexity_metric'] = (X_train['mean concavity'] * X_train['mean concave points']) / (X_train['mean compactness'] + 1e-8)\n    X_test['complexity_metric'] = (X_test['mean concavity'] * X_test['mean concave points']) / (X_test['mean compactness'] + 1e-8)\n    \n    return X_train, X_test\n\n\ndef sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows):\n    return [np.arange(len(X_train))]  # one context view with all training rows\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    return pred","old_string":"\"\"\"Candidate data pipeline around a FROZEN tabular foundation model.\n\nThe harness calls, in order:\n  1. preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test)        -> X_train, y_train, X_test   (cleaning, target transform)\n  2. engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test)          -> X_train, X_test            (feature engineering, <= 500 cols)\n  3. sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows)  -> list of index arrays       (context views; each view is fit separately\n                                                                                 and predictions are averaged)\n  4. frozen model fit/predict per view (never edit this part; MODEL_KWARGS tunes the constructor)\n  5. postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test)     -> pred                       (invert target transforms, calibrate)\n\n`pred` is a pandas DataFrame of class probabilities (columns = class labels) for classification, or a\npandas Series for regression. `y_train_orig` is the untransformed training target. All inputs are pandas\nobjects; X_train / X_test share columns. Do not read any file other than the ones in this directory.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # No preprocessing needed for this dataset\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create engineered features based on domain knowledge\n    \n    # Create ratios between mean and worst for selected key features\n    key_features = ['radius', 'texture', 'perimeter', 'area']\n    for feat in key_features:\n        mean_col = f'mean {feat}'\n        worst_col = f'worst {feat}'\n        if mean_col in X_train.columns and worst_col in X_train.columns:\n            ratio_name = f'{feat}_ratio'\n            X_train[ratio_name] = X_train[mean_col] / (X_train[worst_col] + 1e-8)\n            X_test[ratio_name] = X_test[mean_col] / (X_test[worst_col] + 1e-8)\n    \n    # Create spread features (difference between worst and mean)\n    for feat in ['radius', 'texture', 'perimeter', 'area']:\n        spread_name = f'{feat}_spread'\n        X_train[spread_name] = X_train[f'worst {feat}'] - X_train[f'mean {feat}']\n        X_test[spread_name] = X_test[f'worst {feat}'] - X_test[f'mean {feat}']\n    \n    # Create log-transformed features for skewed distributions\n    skewed_features = ['area', 'perimeter', 'radius']\n    for feat in skewed_features:\n        log_feat = f\"log_{feat}\"\n        X_train[log_feat] = np.log1p(X_train[f'mean {feat}'])\n        X_test[log_feat] = np.log1p(X_test[f'mean {feat}'])\n        \n    # Create a complexity feature based on concavity and concave points\n    X_train['complexity_score'] = (X_train['mean concavity'] * X_train['mean concave points']) / (X_train['mean compactness'] + 1e-8)\n    X_test['complexity_score'] = (X_test['mean concavity'] * X_test['mean concave points']) / (X_test['mean compactness'] + 1e-8)\n    \n    return X_train, X_test\n\n\ndef sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows):\n    return [np.arange(len(X_train))]  # one context view with all training rows\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    return pred"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":32307,"output_tokens":1842,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"total_tokens":34149}}},{"type":"user","uuid":"46fc9008-49ee-4033-adfa-46640fb2c8b1","session_id":"f19a5335-0297-4bcc-a5b4-99e90a6e206a","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_bf9ef2ad38f64d9884fef6de","is_error":false,"content":"The file: /home/yarin.b/projects/excel_magic/artifacts/runs/20261002T174654Z_J6_qwen-code_breast_cancer/workspace/pipeline.py has been updated. Showing lines 23-62 of 69 from the edited file:\n\n---\n\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create engineered features based on domain knowledge for breast cancer classification\n    \n    # Ratio features that might capture differences between benign and malignant tumors\n    # Size ratios\n    X_train['area_perimeter_ratio'] = X_train['mean area'] / (X_train['mean perimeter'] + 1e-8)\n    X_test['area_perimeter_ratio'] = X_test['mean area'] / (X_test[